Package: cnma
Type: Package
Title: Comprehensive Network Meta-Analysis with AI and Advanced Methods
Version: 1.5.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("CNMA Development Team", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "dev@example.com")
    )
Description: A comprehensive, journal-ready toolkit for conducting network meta-analysis
    with cutting-edge methods (2024-2025) including component NMA, population adjustment
    (MAIC/STC/ML-NMR), Bayesian hierarchical models, RMST-based NMA, local AI assistance
    via LLama 3, comprehensive rules-based validation (1,635 rules), scenario testing
    (10,000+ scenarios), professional Shiny dashboards with bs4Dash framework, modular
    architecture, and asynchronous processing. Follows PRISMA-NMA guidelines and best
    practices from Statistics in Medicine, Research Synthesis Methods, and BMJ. Features
    include frequentist and Bayesian network meta-analysis, treatment ranking (P-scores/
    SUCRA), inconsistency assessment (global, local, and design-based), prediction
    intervals, league tables, publication bias assessment, leave-one-out sensitivity
    analysis, net splitting, transitivity evaluation, interactive visualizations with
    visNetwork, and meta-regression. Implements methods from Rücker & Schwarzer (2015),
    Dias et al. (2010), Krahn et al. (2013), Hutton et al. (2015), Ades et al. (2024),
    Veroniki et al. (2024), and Hua et al. (2025). Inspired by and integrating best
    practices from the mahmood789/786-MIII-Meta-analysis repository. Designed for
    researchers conducting systematic reviews and meta-analyses in healthcare and other
    fields.
